    "prior_context": {
      "annotated_sentence_text": "[Turn 4 USER]\ne030\tYou are assuming we can identify a minimal stable format.\ne031\tPriya, who designed the data layer, says that doing so before seeing stranger collections would formalize the wrong abstractions.\ne032\tShe wants public examples precisely to learn what should be stable.\ne033\tOur senior maintainer says that is using users to discover architecture at their expense.\ne034\tThey respect each other, but the conversation has become “learning” versus “responsibility,” and both words are doing too much work.\n[Turn 4 ASSISTANT]\ne035\tThose positions may differ on who bears the cost of uncertainty.\ne036\tPriya expects real use to reveal the right abstractions; the maintainer expects early users to absorb migration and support costs.\ne037\tA release design could make that cost visible and bounded—for example, limiting the beta to disposable projects or providing an export path—yet either choice may reduce the natural use you wanted to observe.\ne038\tThere may not be a way to learn from committed use without creating some obligation to those users.",
